{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Your [B/D#]glory, Lord, is [Esus2]shining [B]bright
Through [G#m7]all that You have [F#sus]made
All [B/D#]chaos fled Your [Esus2]grand [F#sus]design [G#m7]
As [Esus2]beauty [F#sus]took its [B]place
You [Esus2]breathed a word, made [F#sus]rivers burst
You [G#m7]gave the tree of [E]life
The [B]love of God now [Esus2]overflows [B]
Through [B/D#]all that [E]You provide [B]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Your glory shines as we behold
The face of Jesus Christ
His words and deeds have power to flood
Our darkened hearts with light
There on that tree of Calvary
Christ’s life came pouring forth
His death has paid the price for sin
And given us new birth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
We’ll see the glory of our God
When earth has been reborn
The sun and moon will shield their eyes
At the brightness of the Lord
Your bride will feast around that tree
Where healing rivers run
At last the old has passed away
Behold the new has come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Tag}
[B]You are [F#sus]making [G#m7]all things [Esus2]new
{end_of_verse}
